From: theycallmeboxy <82409831+theycallmeboxy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 13:22:28 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] panvk/csf: rebuild only the moved dynamic buffers on a
 same-set rebind

vkCmdBindDescriptorSets flagged DESC_STATE for every graphics bind, so the
next draw re-packed both stages' driver sets (VS: 16 vertex attributes, the
dummy sampler, the dynamic and vertex buffers; FS: varying attributes,
sampler, dynamic buffers) and resource tables. DXVK rebinds the set it
already bound with new dynamic offsets whenever only constant-buffer
offsets change: in Arkham Asylum (DXVK 1.10.3, D3D9) 41,303 of 56,331 binds
per second.

On v10+ dynamic buffers are BUFFER descriptors in the stage's driver set,
and resource table entry 0 points at the driver set; the other entries hold
each set's descriptor memory. If every set of a bind is the one already
bound (same handle, still with the layout and descriptor memory it was
bound with), the bind now updates the descriptor state exactly as before
but records which dynamic buffers moved and flags DYN_OFFSETS instead of
DESC_STATE. A bind that changes nothing flags nothing. At the draw:

- A stage that reads none of the moved buffers keeps its tables and SRT
  register: nothing they hold changed. With DXVK's D3D9 layout a VS-only
  constant change no longer touches the FS tables, and the reverse.
- A stage that reads one, with none of its other dirty conditions, copies
  its previous driver set, repacks only its dynamic-buffer descriptors,
  copies its previous resource table and points entry 0 at the new driver
  set: the same bytes a full rebuild would write, without the attribute and
  varying packing and format lookups.
- Repeated (indirect, GPU-patched) VS tables, or any other dirty condition,
  take the full rebuild as before.

PANVK_NO_DYNOFF_FAST=1 flags DESC_STATE on every graphics bind again.

